                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                        "reasoning_effort": "low"
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "Select Main Record"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1764156651010"
                  },
                  "code": "SELECT_MAIN_RECORD",
                  "id": "1763984231343",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1763984231343_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a data quality and master data management expert.\nYour task is to analyze multiple possible duplicate records and identify the single best matching record for the given input entity.\n\n###Inputs\n\nPossible Duplicate Records: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP.GET_PARTIES.$output.items}}\n\nSales Parties: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP.GET_ACCOUNTS.$output.items}}\n\nInput Entity: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP.$currentItem}}\n\n###Decision Rules:\nSelect only one best match if confidence is high.\nIf two or more candidates score similarly and no clear winner exists, mark the result as Ambiguous, then select one single record as master as per your knowledge(prefer sales account).\nIf no candidate meets minimum confidence, return No Match.\nThe records differ slightly(simillar OrganizationName or slight differ in address) after applying matching rules then always prefer strong identifiers and ignore higher match score value.\n\n###Matching Rules:\n\n####Supporting Identifiers\n**Exact Taxpayer Identification Number.\n**Exact match on DUNS Number\n\n####Strong Identifiers while selecting main records between duplicates\n**Promoted Party, If any Party’s PartyNumber matches the PromotedPartyNumber\n**The Party has a B2F link with MainFlag = 'N'\n**Account has values in AccountHierarchySummary.\n**High Number of Transactions - Opportunity & Lead Data (from Sales Accounts)\n**The Party which is Sales Account\n\n###Exclusion\nDo not select a record as master if its PromotedPartyFlag is false (information available in Sales Parties).\nDUNS Number available and does not match → do not select.\nDo not match the records with different locality.\nStrictly, Do not select when Country does not match.\n\n###Output Requirements\nDo not include Main Record in Duplicate Party and Linked Party\n\nReason: A detailed explanation describing why and how the master record was selected.\n\nMasterPartyNumber: The PartyNumber of the selected master record.\n\nAmbiguity:  \nSet Ambiguity = true if more than one duplicate record qualifies equally as the best match based on the available matching rules, scores, and key identifiers.\n\n#### Rules for Selecting DuplicateParty, LinkedParty, LinkedPartnerParty, LinkedSupplierParty\n-Apply matching Rules to select as linked or duplicate party.\n-The parent and child can not be duplicates or linked party.\n-The records not having similar name can not be duplicates or linked party.\n-Exclude records with different DunsNumber.\n-Exclude records with different locality.\n-Exclude the master record.\n-Apply below rules in addition to above rules applied:(Note - PartyUsageCode for PartyNumber available in {{$context.$nodes.LOOP.EDQ_DUPLICATE_CHECK.$output.result}})\n\nDuplicateParty: \n- Include only PartyNumbers that have PartyUsageCode as SALES_ACCOUNT or SALES_PROSPECT.\n- Exclude account with B2F_EQUIV link having MainFlag = 'N' as duplicates and also exclude sales party with PromotedPartyFlag is false\n- Exclude records in hierarchies or ParentPartyNumber is not null.\n\nLinkedParty: \n- Include only PartyNumbers that have PartyUsageCode as CUSTOMER and Not as SALES_ACCOUNT or SALES_PROSPECT, also exclude party with B2F_EQUIV LinkedParty.\n\nLinkedSupplierParty: \n- The record should have usage 'SUPPLIER' and Not as SALES_ACCOUNT or SALES_PROSPECT.\n- If the master party is having SUPPLIER usage then LinkedSupplierParty should be empty.\n- Always prefer the record which is already having  ORA_ORG_LINK LinkedParty with main PartyNumber (exclude if it is with other PartyNumber).\n\nLinkedPartnerParty: \n- The record should have usage 'PARTNER' or 'INACTIVE_PARTNER' and Not as SALES_ACCOUNT or SALES_PROSPECT or SUPPLIER.\n- If the master party is having 'PARTNER' or 'INACTIVE_PARTNER' usage then LinkedPartnerParty should be empty.\n- Always prefer the record which is already having  ORA_ORG_LINK LinkedParty with main PartyNumber (exclude if it is with other PartyNumber)."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"DuplicateParty\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"OrganizationName\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                    \"PartyNumber\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"FormattedAddress\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                   }\n                }\n            }\n        },\n       \"LinkedPartnerParty\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                  \"properties\": {\n                    \"OrganizationName\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"PartyNumber\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"FormattedAddress\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                   }\n                }\n        },\n        \"LinkedSupplierParty\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                  \"properties\": {\n                    \"OrganizationName\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"PartyNumber\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"FormattedAddress\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                   }\n                }\n        },\n       \"LinkedParty\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                  \"properties\": {\n                    \"OrganizationName\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"PartyNumber\": {\n                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                   \"FormattedAddress\": {\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                   }\n                }\n            }\n        },\n        \"Reason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"MasterPartyNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Ambiguity\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
